WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.066
Expertise should be evaluated with evidence, not status alone.

2
00:00:04.066 --> 00:00:13.101
Job titles, credentials, seniority, and confident explanations can all be useful signals, but they do not always prove reliable performance.

3
00:00:13.101 --> 00:00:19.878
Better evidence includes outcomes, consistency, calibration, prediction quality, decision records, benchmarks, simulations, and scenario exercises.

4
00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:23.492
The question is not simply who sounds persuasive.

5
00:00:23.492 --> 00:00:27.558
The question is who performs well under relevant conditions.

6
00:00:27.558 --> 00:00:29.365
Calibration is especially important.

7
00:00:29.365 --> 00:00:34.786
A calibrated person has confidence that matches actual likelihood, accuracy, or performance.

8
00:00:34.786 --> 00:00:37.949
Poor calibration can appear in two directions.

9
00:00:37.949 --> 00:00:43.822
Someone may be underconfident and fail to act when they have useful knowledge.

10
00:00:43.822 --> 00:00:50.598
Someone else may be overconfident and act with certainty that the evidence does not support.

11
00:00:50.598 --> 00:00:57.827
Expertise includes knowing the difference between what is known, what is likely, and what remains uncertain.

12
00:00:57.827 --> 00:01:03.700
Decision quality is not measured only by whether a single outcome went well.

13
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:09.121
Sometimes a good decision has a bad outcome because conditions were unfavorable.

14
00:01:09.121 --> 00:01:12.735
Sometimes a weak decision succeeds because of luck.

15
00:01:12.735 --> 00:01:26.740
Decision records help teams examine the reasoning that existed at the time: what was known, what assumptions were made, what alternatives were considered, and what evidence would have changed the decision.

16
00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:35.324
Simulations and scenario exercises can reveal expertise because they place people in realistic constraints without waiting for real consequences.

17
00:01:35.324 --> 00:01:39.390
They can test pattern recognition, prioritization, communication, and adaptation.

18
00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:44.359
Benchmarks can also help when they reflect the work that matters.

19
00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:53.394
The best measurements connect to actual performance, not trivia, status, or the ability to explain a process without applying it.
